 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "transactions is an unordered list of rows [transactionId, userId, adDeliveryPennies, paymentPennies, transactionTimestamp] of strings; amounts are decimal integer strings or \"\" (missing, treated as 0) and the timestamp is a decimal integer string. A row adds its ad-delivery amount to the user's balance and subtracts its payment amount. Level 2: given an integer timestamp, use only rows whose timestamp is <= that value and return [userId, balance] for every user with at least one such row, sorted by userId in code-point order.",
